  <static seed="327" source="Library/Michigan/Chap17Sec1/Q19.pg">
    <statement><p>Find a parameterization for the
circle of radius 3
in the <m>xy</m>-plane, centered at the origin,
clockwise.</p>
<p><m>x(t) =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/>,</p>
<p><m>y(t) =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0002"/>,</p>
<p><m>z(t) =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>xy</m>-plane is where <m>z=0</m>, and to make the particle go in
the clockwise direction we start at <m>(3,0,0)</m> and head in the
negative <m>y</m>-direction. Thus one possible answer is
<me>x = 3 \cos t, \quad y = -3 \sin t, \quad z = 0.</me>





</solution>
